---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Work with us — The Breaking Dad"
  description="Brand and PR collaboration enquiries for The Breaking Dad. Based in Hampshire, writing about family life, co-parenting, and product reviews for an engaged UK parent audience."
>
  <div class="static-page">
    <div class="container--narrow">

      <nav class="static-page__breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true"> / </span>
        <span aria-current="page">Work with us</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="static-page__title">Work with us</h1>

      <div class="prose">

        <p>
          The Breaking Dad reaches an engaged audience of UK parents — primarily separated
          or co-parenting mums and dads who are actively looking for practical information,
          honest product recommendations, and content that reflects their actual lives.
          The readership skews heavily mobile, and most of the traffic comes from
          organic search on high-intent queries.
        </p>

        <h2>What I'm open to</h2>
        <p>
          I work with brands on a selective basis. The non-negotiables:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>The product or service has to be something I'd genuinely consider for my own family.</li>
          <li>Editorial independence is not up for negotiation. I write what I actually think.</li>
          <li>Paid coverage is disclosed clearly and honestly. Always.</li>
          <li>I don't do link insertions into existing content for SEO purposes.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Things I'm interested in:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Product reviews</strong> — long-form, honest, based on real-world use over weeks or months. Not a weekend test and a listicle.</li>
          <li><strong>Sponsored content</strong> — written in my voice, clearly disclosed, genuinely useful to my readers.</li>
          <li><strong>Brand partnerships</strong> — where there's a genuine fit with co-parenting, family tech, sustainable home products, or fitness.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Audience</h2>
        <p>
          The majority of readers are UK-based parents aged 28–45. Core topics with the
          highest engagement are separated parenting (co-parenting, benefits, legal rights)
          and product reviews in family tech, footwear, and days out. Traffic is
          predominantly organic and mobile.
        </p>

        <h2>Get in touch</h2>
        <p>
          Drop me a note via the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> with a brief
          overview of what you have in mind. If there's a fit, I'll come back to you quickly.
          If there isn't, I'll say so — no point wasting either of our time.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .static-page {
    padding-block: 2rem 5rem;
  }

  .static-page__breadcrumb {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .static-page__breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .static-page__breadcrumb a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .static-page__title {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: clamp(1.875rem, 5vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
  }
</style>
